Id: ssh021i
Severity: INFO
Category: ssh
Check: check_ssh
Fix: Set DisableForwarding yes (or AllowAgentForwarding no) where users need no agent forwarding.
References: sshd_config(5); ssh-agent(1); CIS Ubuntu Linux 24.04 LTS Benchmark v2.0.0, 5.1.8 (Ensure sshd DisableForwarding is enabled)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-17, IA-2; ISO 8.5, 8.20; CE Secure configuration, User access control

AllowAgentForwarding is yes: a user who connects with agent forwarding
on lends this host their ssh-agent, and root here (or whoever has taken
root) can sign with their keys for as long as the session lasts, and
log in to every host those keys open. It is the default and what every
distribution ships, so INFO; CIS asks for DisableForwarding yes at
Level 2 on servers. As sshd_config(5) says, users with a shell can run
a forwarder of their own, so this protects the careless rather than
stops the determined; the users' side of it is ForwardAgent no in
ssh_config(5), its default too.
